\f1\fs22 Dunhilton dismissed the cabinet. As they rose to leave, he nodded discretely to Gerry who took the seat directly opposite the CEO.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dunhilton grew tense; he had a lot riding on the next few minutes. \'91Operation Parramatta,\'92 he said quietly and emphatically. \'91We can\'92t wait till November now.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Gerry had been dreading this. \'92No, your Serene Corporateness,,\'92 he said reluctantly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We need to act now. 
\f2\i You
\f1\i0  need to act. Whatever you come up with, you will have my complete support.\'92\
